      "updated": 1784201554479,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"messages\": [\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant\"},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Explain very briefly what machine learning is.\"}\n],",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"messages\": [\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant\"},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Explain very briefly what machine learning is.\"}\n],",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "atlYF5p63QGavi4XoXLnm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2425.9455530458836,
      "y": 62499.772100243004,
      "width": 1504.800048828125,
      "height": 1215,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "-GY_y56UTJVLckUo_gtjN",
        "cBnXrZX2oppUxDf5_PFu6",
        "3OSHsMc96y5NGuWDiwrUY"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0E5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1844183138,
      "version": 202,
      "versionNonce": 1584488958,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784201554479,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"<think>\\n\n    Okay, the user wants a brief explanation of machine learning.\n    Let me start by recalling what I know. \n    Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence where \n    algorithms learn from data to make predictions or decisions without \n    being explicitly programmed. \\n\\nI should mention that it's about \n    training models on data to improve their accuracy over time. \n    Maybe use an analogy to make it relatable. Like, a doctor using \n    patient data to predict diseases. \n    Also, explain the key components: data, algorithms, training, \n    and evaluation. \\n\\n\n\n    Wait, the user asked for it very briefly. So I need to keep it concise. \n    Avoid jargon. Make sure to highlight that it's not about programming \n    but about learning from data. Maybe add that it's used in various \n    fields like healthcare, finance, etc. \\n\\n\n\n    Let me check if I'm missing anything. Oh, right, the main idea is \n    that models improve with more data. That's important. Alright, \n    structure it with a definition, components, and application. \n    Keep sentences simple. Alright, that should cover it.\\n\n</think>\\n\\n\n\nMachine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence where \nalgorithms learn patterns from data to make decisions or predictions\n without being explicitly programmed. It involves training models \non data to improve accuracy over time.\"",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"<think>\\n\n    Okay, the user wants a brief explanation of machine learning.\n    Let me start by recalling what I know. \n    Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence where \n    algorithms learn from data to make predictions or decisions without \n    being explicitly programmed. \\n\\nI should mention that it's about \n    training models on data to improve their accuracy over time. \n    Maybe use an analogy to make it relatable. Like, a doctor using \n    patient data to predict diseases. \n    Also, explain the key components: data, algorithms, training, \n    and evaluation. \\n\\n\n\n    Wait, the user asked for it very briefly. So I need to keep it concise. \n    Avoid jargon. Make sure to highlight that it's not about programming \n    but about learning from data. Maybe add that it's used in various \n    fields like healthcare, finance, etc. \\n\\n\n\n    Let me check if I'm missing anything. Oh, right, the main idea is \n    that models improve with more data. That's important. Alright, \n    structure it with a definition, components, and application. \n    Keep sentences simple. Alright, that should cover it.\\n\n</think>\\n\\n\n\nMachine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence where \nalgorithms learn patterns from data to make decisions or predictions\n without being explicitly programmed. It involves training models \non data to improve accuracy over time.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
